| 2018 | Prelims | President's veto powers | Veto | Absolute, suspensive, pocket; no qualified veto; money bills limited |
| 2019 | Prelims | Pardoning power difference between President and Governor | Pardoning | President can pardon death sentence and court martial; Governor cannot pardon death sentence |
| 2020 | Mains | Constitutional position of President - nominal vs real executive | Position | Art. 74, 44th Amendment, situational discretion |

### 17.11. CURRENT AFFAIRS LINKAGE (2023-2026)

| Issue | Linkage | Mains Angle |
|---|---|---|
| Use of ordinance route by governments | Art. 123 | Frequent promulgation, need for legislative scrutiny, D.C. Wadhwa principles |
| Presidential references and clemency petitions | Art. 72, Art. 143 | Death penalty jurisprudence, mercy petitions, delay concerns |
| Role of President in hung assemblies/government formation | Situational discretion | Constitutional conventions, Sarkaria/Bommai principles |

