## 18. VICE-PRESIDENT

**[SYL: GS2-C.1] | [LAXMIKANTH: Chapter 18] | [BARE ACT: Arts. 63-73]**

### 18.1. Introduction

Vice-President is second highest office in India, ranked next to President in official warrant of precedence. Modelled on American Vice-President.

### 18.2. Election (Art. 66)

Elected by **indirect election** by electoral college consisting of **members of both Houses of Parliament (elected and nominated)**. **Not** elected by State Legislatures (unlike President). 

**Election system:** Proportional representation by **single transferable vote**, secret ballot (same as President). All doubts/disputes decided by **Supreme Court** - final. If election declared void, acts done before declaration remain valid.

### 18.3. Qualifications, Oath, Conditions (Arts. 66, 69)

**Qualifications:** Citizen of India, completed 35 years of age, qualified for election as **member of Rajya Sabha**, must not hold any office of profit (exemptions similar to President).

**Oath (Art. 69):** Administered by President or person appointed by him. Swears to bear true faith and allegiance to Constitution, uphold sovereignty/integrity of India, and faithfully discharge duties of office.

**Conditions:** Must not be member of Parliament or State Legislature (if elected, seat deemed vacant); cannot hold any other office of profit.

### 18.4. Term, Removal, Vacancy (Arts. 67, 68)

**Term:** 5 years from date of assuming office. Can resign by writing to **President**. Can hold office beyond term till successor assumes charge.

**Removal:** Removed by resolution of **Rajya Sabha** passed by **effective majority** (majority of total membership) and agreed to by **Lok Sabha** by simple majority (Art. 67(b)). No formal impeachment like President; no ground specified in Constitution. **14 days' notice** required.

**Vacancy:** Occurs by expiry of term, resignation, removal, death or otherwise. Election to fill vacancy held **as soon as possible**, newly elected VP remains in office for **full 5-year term**.

### 18.5. Powers and Functions

**Ex-officio Chairman of Rajya Sabha (Art. 64):** Primary function is to preside over Rajya Sabha. Acts as Chairman, not as member of Rajya Sabha. While presiding, has same powers as Speaker of Lok Sabha re: preserving order, casting vote in case of tie.

**Acting President (Art. 65):** When President's office vacant or President unable to discharge functions, VP acts as President. During this period, VP **ceases** to perform duties as Chairman of Rajya Sabha; Deputy Chairman of Rajya Sabha presides. While acting as President, VP has all powers/immunities of President and is entitled to President's emoluments/allowances (not VP's).

**Other functions:** Performs functions as assigned by President or Parliament by law. No other constitutional functions when not acting as President.

### 18.6. COMPARISON: INDIAN VP vs AMERICAN VP

| Aspect | Indian VP | American VP |
|---|---|---|
| **Election** | Elected by Parliament (both Houses, elected+nominated) only | Elected by electoral college same as President (with popular vote element) |
| **State Legislatures** | Not involved | Not directly involved but part of same electoral college system |
| **Primary Role** | Ex-officio Chairman of Rajya Sabha | President of Senate (largely ceremonial); more significant as potential successor |
| **Acting as Head of State** | Acts as President only in vacancy/incapacity (temporary) | Becomes President on vacancy (succeeds fully) |
| **Removal** | By resolution of Rajya Sabha (effective majority) + Lok Sabha agreement (simple majority) | By impeachment same as President |

### 18.7. PYQs (PRELIMS) - QUICK REVISION

| Year | Question | Answer |
|---|---|---|
| 2016 | Vice-President is elected by? | Members of both Houses of Parliament (elected and nominated) |
| 2017 | Vice-President acts as President when? | On vacancy or inability of President to discharge functions |
| 2019 | Removal of Vice-President requires resolution by? | Rajya Sabha by effective majority, agreed to by Lok Sabha by simple majority |

### 18.8. MIND MAP

```text
VICE-PRESIDENT (ARTS. 63-73)
├── ELECTION
│   ├── By electoral college of both Houses of Parliament (elected + nominated)
│   ├── PR by single transferable vote, secret ballot
│   └── Not by State Legislatures
├── QUALIFICATIONS
│   ├── Citizen, 35 years, qualified for Rajya Sabha, no office of profit
│   └── Oath administered by President
├── TERM & REMOVAL
│   ├── 5 years, resign to President, re-electable
│   └── Removed by RS (effective majority) + LS agreement (simple majority), 14 days notice
└── FUNCTIONS
    ├── Ex-officio Chairman of Rajya Sabha
    └── Acts as President when vacancy/incapacity (then ceases as RS Chairman)
```

