## 21. CABINET COMMITTEES

**[SYL: GS2-C.1] | [LAXMIKANTH: Chapter 21]**

### 21.1. Introduction

Cabinet Committees are **extra-constitutional** bodies (not mentioned in Constitution) but are part of Westminster model. They are set up by **Prime Minister** to reduce workload of Cabinet by taking decisions on specific matters. Decisions of Cabinet Committees are normally binding on Cabinet.

### 21.2. Features
- Set up by PM by modifying rules of business
- Extra-constitutional
- Comprise Cabinet Ministers
- Usually chaired by PM (or senior minister)
- Reduce Cabinet workload through delegation
- Decisions binding, reported to Cabinet if required

### 21.3. Important Cabinet Committees (current structure varies)

| Committee | Purpose |
|---|---|
| **Cabinet Committee on Security (CCS)** | Defence, national security, atomic energy policy, issues relating to war/peace |
| **Cabinet Committee on Political Affairs (CCPA)** | Policy matters related to domestic political issues |
| **Cabinet Committee on Economic Affairs (CCEA)** | Economic policy, foreign investment, price control etc. |
| **Appointments Committee of the Cabinet (ACC)** | Appointments to posts of Chairman/MDs of PSUs, Secretary-level appointments etc. |
| **Cabinet Committee on Investment and Growth** | To expedite investment projects (varies over time) |
| **Cabinet Committee on Accommodation** | Allocation of government accommodation |
| **Cabinet Committee on Parliamentary Affairs** | Scrutinizes legislative program, advises on parliamentary strategy |

### 21.4. Groups of Ministers (GoMs) & Empowered Groups of Ministers (EGoMs)

**GoMs** set up by Cabinet for specific issues; recommendations to Cabinet.
**EGoMs** empowered to take decisions on behalf of Cabinet in specified matters (introduced to speed up decisions). Since 2014, practice of EGoMs/GoMs has been **scaled down** in favour of other mechanisms.

### 21.5. PYQs

| Year | Exam | Question | Topic | Approach |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 2017 | Prelims | Cabinet Committee on Security deals with? | CCS | Defence, national security, war/peace |
| 2018 | Prelims | Cabinet Committees are constitutional or extra-constitutional? | Nature | Extra-constitutional, set up by PM |

### 21.6. MIND MAP

```text
CABINET COMMITTEES
├── Extra-constitutional, set up by PM
├── Reduce Cabinet workload
├── Key Committees: CCS, CCEA, CCPA, ACC
└── Decisions normally binding on Cabinet
```

